     I saw Mr. Sevarian's message re: an axe named Cleaver, and figured: "Oh!
That's because an axe doesn't do much damage."  I wrote a message, found I
had refuted almost all the claims I had made in the first 20 or so lines when
I had written the second 20 or so lines, and decided to throw it out.
     What I found was that I don't know how to interpret my tables for
weapons.  I have, essentially, three difficulties:
1. The weapons and named weapons tables refer to an "Sdam" and an "Ldam."
My two hypotheses here are:
   A. That "S" and "L" refer to "short" and "long" as in range.  This
   seems inconsistant with that Excalibur has a +5S and a +10L bonus.  While
   in Gauntlet Valkries throw their longswords, that doesn't seem like the
   Nethack way to go.
   B. That they refer to "small" and "large" monsters.  This is consistant
   with that "Snickersnee" has a +0S and +8L bonus, but not especially
   so with that "Ogresmasher" has a +5S and +0L bonus.
   Oh, I suppose I could add: C. Hit and damage.  But I haven't the slightest
   what "s" and "l" would stand for, nor the reference to "S" as "Sdam."
2. The weapons table refers to these two damages as numbers, and then by
   the side of some weapons says "+d6 Sdam" or some such figure.  Are the
   base figures constants, or maximums?
3. Most of the "Special features" column baffles me.  Why doesn't the game
   say when fire damage, cold damage, or electrical damage is occurring, if
   it is?  What is "Defender"?  And, most confusingly, what does the "slay X"
   attribute do?  Does it double the damage to that particular class of
   monster, or only add damage against that monster, or what?


